question: 20, answer 160 {'source': 'What environment has low rainfall?\n\nChoices:\n- tropics\n- sandy zone\n- sandbox\n- forests', 'target': 'sandy zone', 'rationale': "The sandy zone is a dry environment, with low rainfall and water scarcity. The definition of the sandbox is not clear from the context provided; hence, it cannot be considered as an answer choice for this question. Tropics are areas that lie close to the tropic circles – which represent regions on Earth where there’s maximum solar radiation received during specific equinoxes or solstices (e.g., summer solstice). These environments receive high amounts of sunlight, but their rainfalls vary depending on location – some tropical regions experience heavy rains while others have drought-like conditions in certain months out of the year. Forests generally don't get too much sunshine because they're covered by trees, so they typically do not fit into any sand zones either", 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
