question: 108, answer 122 {'source': "In this task, you are given a multiple-choice question about healthcare. Answer the question based on your information and classify your answers into '1', '2', '3', and '4'.\n\nQuestion: Alveolar pressure exceeds atmospheric pressure: \n Options:  <1> In the initial phase of inspiration. <2> In the middle phase of inspiration. <3> In the middle phase of an expiration. <4> At the end of expiration. <5> At the end of the inspiration.", 'target': '3', 'rationale': 'The alveoli are filled with air during inspiration, so the alveolar pressure is slightly lower than atmospheric pressure. This difference in pressure causes the air to flow into the lungs. During expiration, the diaphragm and intercostal muscles relax, increasing intra-thoracic volume and decreasing intrapulmonary volume. The decrease in intrapulmonary volume increases alveolar pressure above that of atmospheric pressure causing air to move out of the lung through exhalation. Therefore, option 3 is correct because it states that alveolar pressure exceeds atmospheric only during expiration.', 'task': 'head_qa', 'type': 'CoT'}
