question: 60, answer 139 {'source': 'Which plant absorbs the most sunlight?\n\nA -> the one that dates grow on\n\nB -> the one that eats insects\n\nC -> the one that grows in the tundra\n\nD -> the one that ladybugs like the best\n\nIs the right answer A, B, C or D ?', 'target': 'A', 'rationale': '"The one that dates grow on" is a palm tree. Palm trees absorb the most sunlight of any plant in tropical regions where they are found, especially desert date palms which can survive extreme temperatures and reflect very little light off their leaves due to their waxy coating.\nIn comparison, insectivorous plants do not rely as heavily on absorbing sunlight since they also get energy from digesting insects, while tundra vegetation only needs enough energy for basic survival during harsh winters because there\'s no sun at all during those months anyway. Ladybugs have nothing to do with how much sunlight a plant absorbs so D doesn\'t make sense either. So A is definitely correct here.""', 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
