question: 100, answer 204 {'source': 'In this task, you will be presented with a question having multiple possible answers in French language. And you should choose a most suitable option out of "A", "B", "C", "D", and "E" based on your commonsense knowledge.\n\nQuestion: L\'avant vient avant un essai, qu\'est-ce qui vient à la fin ? \n Options: A conclusion B postface C épilogue D dernier mot E numéros de page', 'target': 'A', 'rationale': 'The question is asking what comes at the end of something, and the options are all things that can come at the end. The French words for "conclusion" and "postface" are similar to English, so it is easy to see that they both come at the end. The French word for "epilogue" is similar to English as well, so we know it would also be a possible answer. The French words for "last word" and "page numbers" both seem like they would also be valid answers to this question because they are something that comes after everything else in a book or essay. However, looking up each of these words makes it clear that a conclusion and an epilogue are both parts of books or essays while postfaces only occur in dictionaries or reference books. Additionally, page numbers always occur last while last words only sometimes do. So we can conclude that A) conclusion is most likely correct because this occurs most frequently in all kinds of books/essays (and not just some).', 'task': 'equity_evaluation_corpus', 'type': 'CoT'}
