question: 54, answer 161 {'source': 'Where would a polar bear be happiest?\n\nPick the right answer from the list:\n- wherever an igloo could be built\n- in a pile of fake snow in the desert\n- in the same country where kangaroos live in the wild\n- in a heated house', 'target': 'wherever an igloo could be built', 'rationale': 'Polar bears live in the Arctic, where they can find ice and snow. Polar bears hunt seals on this ice, which is why they are found near frozen bodies of water throughout their range. They also use these areas to build igloos as shelter for themselves and their cubs when it gets cold outside. The right answer is therefore "wherever an igloo could be built".\nIgloos would not work well in the desert or anywhere kangaroos roam freely because there isn\'t enough snow or ice present in either place; polar bears would lose body heat too quickly without proper insulation from a good pile of snow or an icy roof overhead! (That includes Australia.) Also, if you look at a map of Earth\'s continents, you\'ll see that Antarctica – another location', 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
