question: 79, answer 133 {'source': 'The state of a gas vaporized from a surface liquid under increased pressure and higher temperatures is\n\nPick the right answer from the list:\n- part of how nature replenishes, purifies and recirculates water\n- a stage when water molecules are prevented from escaping into the atmosphere\n- a stage when moisture leaves the atmosphere without being recirculated\n- a stage that only occurs once', 'target': 'part of how nature replenishes, purifies and recirculates water', 'rationale': "Water vapor is the gas state of water. It is created when liquid water evaporates, or changes from a liquid to a gaseous state. Water molecules can change states because they have energy in them due to their molecular bonds and structure.\nOnce this energy increases sufficiently that it causes some of the molecules to break free, evaporation occurs as these freed molecules go on into the atmosphere above Earth's surface where they may be rescued by clouds (where precipitation will soon follow) or perhaps other processes within nature’s hydrological cycle; that being part of how nature replenishes, purifies and recirculates water around us all.", 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
