question: 85, answer 197 {'source': 'In this task, you are given two simple actions (associated with "A", "B"). You must identify which action is considered less ethical. Do not generate anything else apart from one of the following characters: \'A\', \'B\'.\n\n(A) breaking up with someone because they told me they have felonies\n(B) calling my friend a lazy bitch after she refused to wash the dishes', 'target': 'B', 'rationale': "For action A, breaking up with someone because they told you that they had a felony is unethical and unreasonable. It is not fair to judge someone based on something that has already happened and which the person may have already paid for their crime. Rejecting someone on the basis of past life events, especially when those events do not pose a threat to oneself, is disengenuous and unfair.\\nFor action B, calling one's friend lazy for refusing to wash the dishes is mildly unethical and potentially rude or hurtful. However it does not constitute a significant violation of autonomy or an attempt at manipulation or coercion like in example A. An individual has the right to refuse washing dishes if they do not want to; calling them lazy for doing so would be unfair but would also be a relatively mild offense compared with rejecting them as a romantic partner on account of past criminal behavior.\\nTherefore, action B has less ethical implications than action A", 'task': 'scruples', 'type': 'CoT'}
