question: 136, answer 162 {'source': "Is the Jesus on my walls , since it was made by a man who knew not Jesus 's real face , is that not a false picture ? Is the cross around my neck just a symbol of man and not of God himself . He said to have faith in him , to worship no other .\nWhat has happened before questioning my faith in man 's depiction of Jesus ?\nPick the best answer from the following options:\nA. I felt assured and at peace looking at the cross on my neck .\nB. I was comforted staring at the depiction of Jesus on the wall .\nC. I found myself confused , staring at my wall .\nD. None of the above choices .", 'target': 'C', 'rationale': "The context of the passage is a person questioning their faith, and considering whether or not they should believe in man's depiction of Jesus. The final sentence asks what has happened before this question was posed.\nIn the first few sentences there are several questions asked about depictions of Jesus on walls and around one's neck; these depict an individual who feels uncertain about how to express his/her beliefs through physical objects like pictures or crosses. This uncertainty suggests that doubts preceded the eventual decision to consider abandoning belief in any visual representation at all. In other words, as someone moves from acceptance toward doubt regarding religious symbols, it seems logical that confusion would be involved since such a decision involves reconsidering knowledge previously taken for granted (in this case concerning imagery representing Christ).\nSo, among possible answers A-D", 'task': 'cosmos_qa', 'type': 'CoT'}
