question: 17, answer 123 {'source': 'Q: What is the scientific term for the act of eating or feeding?\n\n\nA:', 'target': 'ingestion', 'rationale': "The definition of the word “digestion” is the process by which food and drink are broken down into their smallest parts so that our bodies can use them to build new cells. Ingestion begins when we eat something, while digestion actually starts in the mouth with chewing and ends when leftover waste passes out through your anus as stool. \nIngestion occurs at all stages of eating a meal: from putting food in one's mouth to swallowing it; whereas ingestion only applies to taking things like vitamins or supplements orally (by mouth).\nSo, answer is: ingestion", 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
