question: 109, answer 137 {'source': 'In this task, you need to provide the correct option for a given problem from the provided options.\n\nProblem: in a chess competition involving some men and women , every player needs to play exactly one game with every other player . it was found that in 45 games , both the players were women and in 190 games , both players were men . what is the number of games in which one person was a man and other person was a woman ? \nOptions: a ) 40 , b ) 120 , c ) 180 , d ) 200 , e ) 220', 'target': 'd', 'rationale': 'The total number of games played in the tournament would be given by nC2 where n is the total number of players. Here, n = 45 + 190 = 235. So, total number of games will be 235C2 = 23465.\\nNow we have to find the number of games in which one player was a man and another was a woman. We know that there were 45 matches between women and 190 matches between men, so there would have been (45+190)C2 - (45)C2 - (190)C2 = 4420 matches with 1 man and 1 woman as players.\\nSo, the answer would be 4420 [or 200].', 'task': 'mathqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
