question: 33, answer 141 {'source': 'Q: Ringworm and athlete’s foot are common human diseases caused by types of what?\n\n\n Choices:\n\n- viruses\n\n- multicellular bacteria\n\n- acids\n\n- fungi\n\nA:', 'target': 'fungi', 'rationale': 'Ringworm and athlete’s foot are fungal infections that cause raised, ring-shaped rashes on the skin. These diseases affect humans but can also infect other animals like cats and dogs. Ringworm is caused by a group of fungi called dermatophytes, which means “skin plant." Athlete’s foot is a similar infection in the same family as ringworm known scientifically as tinea pedis or commonly referred to simply as "jock itch".\nThe question asks what causes human disease; thus viruses, bacteria (multicellular or not), acids don\'t fit with this description. Fungi do cause these conditions so it must be correct choice therefore answer should be fungi', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
