question: 83, answer 108 {'source': 'I gave my students this multiple choice question: Most volcanoes develop due to interactions between two tectonic plates. Which of the tectonic plate interactions is least likely to produce volcanic activity?\n\nOnly one answer is correct among these 4 choices:\n- two diverging oceanic plates\n- two converging oceanic plates\n- two diverging continental plates\n- two converging continental plates\n\nCould you tell me which one is correct?', 'target': 'two converging continental plates', 'rationale': 'volcanoes are formed when tectonic plates move apart or collide. Divergent and converging boundaries can both produce volcanoes, but divergent boundaries usually form chains of volcanoes on land while converging plate margins create mountain ranges (usually with active volcanism). Volcanic activity is more frequent along the oceanic ridges than at subduction zones because there is less friction where two plates slide past each other compared to a collision between two thick continental masses\nTherefore, "two converging continental plates" should be selected as the correct answer.', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Challenge', 'type': 'CoT'}
