question: 45, answer 155 {'source': 'A type of bird in Africa eats blood-sucking insects off large mammals. Which word best describes the relationship between the bird and the mammals?\n\nOptions:\n- mutualism\n- parasitism\n- neutralism\n- commensalism', 'target': 'mutualism', 'rationale': 'The word that best describes the relationship between a bird in Africa and large mammals is mutualism.\nMutualism refers to a type of symbiosis, which occurs when two organisms live together with benefits for both parties involved. \nIn this case, the mammal provides food (i.e., insects) while being protected from harmful parasites by birds who eat them off their bodies. Both species benefit from each other so it can be argued that this form of coexistence is an example of mutualistic behavior or mutualism relationship.\n\n\nwww[dot]britannica[dot]com/science/symbiotic-relationship#ref585287\n\n\nhttps://study[dot]com/academy/lesson/mutualism-in-the-rain', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Challenge', 'type': 'CoT'}
