question: 136, answer 164 {'source': 'Q: What is the blastocyst called after implantation?\n\n\nRead this paragraph and choose the correct option from the provided answers:\n\nAfter implantation occurs, the blastocyst is called an embryo . The embryonic stage lasts through the eighth week following fertilization. During this time, the embryo grows in size and becomes more complex. It develops specialized cells and tissues and starts to form most organs. For an interactive animation of embryonic development, go to this link: http://health. howstuffworks. com/adam-200129. htm .\n\n Choices:\n\n- trophoblast\n\n- an nucleus\n\n- an produce\n\n- an embryo\n\n\nA:', 'target': 'an embryo', 'rationale': 'The paragraph describes the implantation process, which involves an egg being fertilized and implanted in a uterus. After this occurs, the blastocyst is called an embryo. The embryonic stage lasts through the eighth week following fertilization. During this time, it grows in size and becomes more complex. It develops specialized cells and tissues and starts to form most organs.\nSo, based on all of these details provided by the text above, we can conclude that after implantation occurs: \n\n - trophoblast cannot be correct because it refers to tissue formed from outer layer of cells surrounding inner cell mass during development of blastula; as defined before at https://en . wikipedia . org/wiki/Trophoblast\n - nucleus is not correct because it refers either to membrane-', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
