question: 128, answer 160 {'source': 'Read the following paragraph and determine if the hypothesis is true. Select from options at the end:\n\nMr. Bush warned opposition Democrats in Congress against raising taxes, saying that is the worst thing lawmakers could do. But he did urge them to pass legislation that could help more Americans refinance their homes. "When Congress comes back, I look forward to working with them to deal with the economic realities of the moment and to ensure the American people that we will do everything we can to make sure we remain a prosperous country," he added.\n\nHypothesis: The Congress wants to boost the economy.\nOPTIONS:\n- yes\n- no\nThe answer is', 'target': 'no', 'rationale': "The statement “Mr. Bush warned opposition Democrats in Congress against raising taxes, saying that is the worst thing lawmakers could do” highlights how Mr. Bush does not agree with his opponents on dealing with economic issues and as such there may be internal disagreements about what to do for boosting the economy. Hence, it cannot be said that everything will be done to ensure prosperity of America or else Mr. Bush would have stated so during this critical time of crisis where he has already been criticised heavily by the Opposition parties for being unable to take adequate measures earlier on when recession was looming large over America's head (which can also be validated from a prior sentence stating “Lawmakers are considering another package worth $150 billion which includes tax cuts aimed at helping businesses and middle-income Americans buy new homes", 'task': 'rte', 'type': 'CoT'}
