question: 73, answer 110 {'source': "Here's a problem to solve: Which statement describes animal embryos?\n\nAmong the 4 following options, which is the correct answer?\n\n- A: display all the features of an adult\n \n- B: represent the earliest stage of development\n \n- C: have the same number of cells as a fertilized egg\n \n- D: have half the number of chromosomes as an adult", 'target': 'B', 'rationale': 'In animals, an embryo is the stage of development that follows fertilization. Developmental biology considers embryos to be in their earliest stages and thus represent the first level of organization.\nAn animal embryo has all the genetic information necessary for its further growth and differentiation into a mature adult organism, however it does not have any recognizable features at this developmental stage as these are acquired during later periods of embryogenesis. \nAmong options A-D provided above, only option B correctly answers which statement described animal embryos best: "represent the earliest stage of development".', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Easy', 'type': 'CoT'}
