question: 59, answer 151 {'source': 'Question: A Motorcycle and an SUV are stopped at a stop light. When the light turns green which vehicle gets the jump on the other? (A) Suv (B) Motorcycle\n\nDo not use A and B to answer the question but instead, choose between "Motorcycle" and  "SUV".', 'target': 'SUV', 'rationale': 'As the SUV has a greater mass than motorcycle, it will require more force to accelerate. But as both vehicles are equally likely to have an engine of equal power, they will apply their maximum possible forces simultaneously and hence reach their respective max speeds at the same time.\nSo if we consider that those two were stopped for about 5 seconds then when light turns green:\n- Motorcycle would be able to attain its max speed within 1 second or less after starting from 0 mph (or kmph). So lets say it is approx 20 m/s(motorcycles can go faster but let’s take this conservative number) . This means in first 5 sec bike would cover 100 meters so that by 6th second it reaches stoplight again. \n- An SUV takes time proportional', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
