question: 54, answer 151 {'source': 'At a campsite one night we all gather round a fire to roast marshmallows; this is an example of\n\nA -> dinner\n\nB -> fusion\n\nC -> maillard reaction\n\nD -> competition\n\nIs the right answer A, B, C or D ?', 'target': 'C', 'rationale': 'The Maillard reaction is a chemical reaction between amino acids and reducing sugars that gives browned food its distinctive flavor. When something burns, it undergoes the combustion process which releases energy in the form of heat or light; this causes carbonisation. The charring on burnt toast, for example, is an example of carbonisation occurring as a result of combustion: initially glucose (a sugar) reacts with oxygen to produce water vapour and carbon dioxide gas releasing some energy as visible light through incandescence but also causing heating so other reactions are initiated including caramelization - decomposition/burning-of sucrose into products such as furfural giving rise to more complex flavours than those produced by Maillard alone.\nSo C maillards reaction', 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
