question: 61, answer 134 {'source': 'Here\'s a logic test: Mary noticed that her pencil got hotter when rubbing it in sandpaper than when rubbing it in cloth. Does the _____ have more resistance? (A) sandpaper or (B) cloth\n\nChoose the answer between "sandpaper" and "cloth".', 'target': 'sandpaper', 'rationale': 'According to the law of conservation of energy, energy can\'t be created or destroyed. This means that when you rub a pencil over sandpaper and then cloth, the kindling friction will produce heat both times but in different quantities because some materials are better conductors than others. Sandpaper has more resistance as it provides greater frictional opposition compared to fabric so is less conducive allowing for little electrical current flow and higher temperature generation due to its roughness causing increased collision between particles relative to cloth which has low resistance permitting easier passage through it with minimal particle interaction thus generating lesser amounts of heat during pencile rubbing action.\n \nSo the answer is "sandpaper".', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
