question: 46, answer 120 {'source': 'I gave my students this multiple choice question: Which object best reflects light?\n\nOnly one answer is correct among these 4 choices:\n- gray door\n- white floor\n- black sweater\n- brown carpet\n\nCould you tell me which one is correct?', 'target': 'white floor', 'rationale': "All objects and surfaces will reflect some light, but in general the more opaque or shiny a surface is, the greater its ability to reflect.\nThe white floor reflects all wavelengths of visible light equally well and so appears white; it's not that other colors are absorbed. The brown carpet absorbs little red-orange color from illumination (the bulb may be emitting very little anyhow at those wavelengths) because it can't absorb them with only weak absorption bands for such long wavelength electromagnetic radiation which means they're reflected as seen by our eyes . Therefor , this answer choice is incorrect .", 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Easy', 'type': 'CoT'}
