question: 81, answer 122 {'source': 'Q: Air temperature changes as what increases?\n\n\nRead this paragraph and choose the correct option from the provided answers:\n\nAir temperature changes as altitude increases. In some layers of the atmosphere, the temperature decreases. In other layers, it increases. You can see this in Figure below . Refer to this figure as you read about the layers below.\n\n Choices:\n\n- pressure\n\n- density\n\n- salinity\n\n- altitude\n\n\nA:', 'target': 'altitude', 'rationale': 'The passage is about the layers of the atmosphere and how their temperatures change as altitude increases. The figure shows that air temperature either decreases or increases with changes in altitude, so choice (A) is incorrect. \nPressure refers to force applied per unit area; density measures mass per volume; and salinity describes salt content relative to water content. None of these concepts are related to air temperature, so choices (B), (C), and (D) are also incorrect. Therefore, by process of elimination, we know that only choice (E) can be correct: Air temperature changes as altitude increases.', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
