question: 138, answer 163 {'source': "Read the following article and select the best answer.\nArticle: Four friends live in a small town. Their names are Cook, Miller, Smith, and Carter. They have different jobs. One is a policeman, one is a carpenter , one is a farmer, and one is a doctor. One day Cook's son broke  his right leg, and Cook took him to the doctor. The doctor's sister is Smith's wife. The farmer isn't married . He has a lot of good hens. Miller always buys eggs from the farmer. The policeman sees Smith every day because they are neighbors .\nQuestion: Who is a policeman?\n- Cook\n- Smith\n- Miller\n- Cart", 'target': 'Cook', 'rationale': 'The article discusses the lives of four friends in a small town. Cook is described as having taken his son to a doctor, while Smith has an occupation that requires him to have medical training (doctor). This suggests that Smith is likely the person who treated Cook\'s injured son.\nBased on this evidence, it can be inferred that since Miller did not treat Cook\'s injured son and Carter was not mentioned at all in relation to any injuries or treating them, they are less likely candidates for being the policeman than Cook. It seems probable then that police work involves investigating accidents like broken legs and might also require interacting with doctors about such cases; either way it makes sense for these two professions to interact frequently which explains why Smith sees Cook every day because they are neighbors . Hence "Cook" would be most', 'task': 'race@middle', 'type': 'CoT'}
