question: 34, answer 155 {'source': 'What time are you most likely to see a rainbow\n- 10:00 A.M.\n- 9:00 P.M.\n- 3 A.M.\n- Midnight', 'target': '10:00 A.M.', 'rationale': 'Rainbows typically form after rainfall. If we look at a rainbow, the light is refracted by water droplets in the air when it hits them from behind us (meaning the sun must be on our side of the rainbow). Water will therefore not obstruct sunlight until later in the day if rain occurs during that time period. Additionally, clouds may move into an area and block out any opportunity to see even part of a rainbow. So assuming there was heavy rain overnight, you are most likely to wake up early and head outside around 10:00 A.M., where you can still enjoy bright sunshine without additional cloud cover getting in your way!\nSo I think this question should have 9:00 P.M as answer instead of 10 A.M', 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
