question: 98, answer 165 {'source': 'Goal: How to stuff egg carton to make fire starter.\n\nWhich is the correct ending?\n- Using dryer lint, fill each slot of egg carton with the lint. When full, drop wax over each hole where the lint is located. Wait to solidify.\n- Using belly lint, fill each slot of egg carton with the lint. When full, drop wax over each hole where the lint is located. Wait to solidify.\n\nAnswer:', 'target': 'Using dryer lint, fill each slot of egg carton with the lint. When full, drop wax over each hole where the lint is located. Wait to solidify.', 'rationale': 'The correct answer is "Using dryer lint, fill each slot of egg carton with the lint. When full, drop wax over each hole where the lint is located. Wait to solidify." because it makes sense in terms of what -are- fire starters and how they are made:\nFire starters consist commonly out of some sort flammable material that can be easily ignited (i.e., a cardboard), which will then light something else (like logs or sticks) on fire much more efficiently than trying to do so by itself. To make this work well you want a highly combustible substance, like cotton fibers from clothes we wear ("dryer lint"). The other choice have no such purpose as part of making your own fire starter at home; however belly', 'task': 'piqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
