question: 144, answer 168 {'source': "In this task, you're given four sentences of a story written in natural language. The given story is not complete and your job is to complete the story by selecting one of the sentence choices from (A) and (B), such that the story sounds fully coherent.\n\nSentence1: My friend and I had a little contest the other day. Sentence2: We tried to see who could blow the biggest bubblegum bubble. Sentence3: We took different turns and would take measurements. Sentence4: When his was getting at it's biggest I popped it. \n (A) He was a little mad, but I just laughed. (B) He never did understand the best way to fry an egg.", 'target': 'A', 'rationale': 'The story starts by stating that the protagonist and their friend had a little contest. The next sentence describes the task (blowing the biggest bubblegum bubble), which makes sense given that it was a contest. Additionally, the second sentence includes measurements, which means there were winners and losers for this particular competition. In Sentence3, we learn that they took turns with different measurements being taken. This implies that one of them would end up winning and one would end up losing. Finally, in Sentence4 we learn of an action by the protagonist that could be viewed as cheating or unsportsmanlike conduct (popping his competitor\'s bubble). Given these details about the story thus far, it is most likely to make sense if we choose option A because it describes how he responded to her cheating ("He was a little mad").', 'task': 'roc_stories', 'type': 'CoT'}
