question: 77, answer 123 {'source': 'Choose between "concrete floor" and  "carpeted floor".\nQuestion: Kate is at the movies and drops her cup on the floor accidentally. The cup rolls away very quickly on the concrete floor, but it slows down once it hits the carpeted floor. The cup was faster on the concrete floor because the concrete floor had (A) more friction (B) less friction.', 'target': 'carpeted floor', 'rationale': 'A concrete floor and a carpeted floor have different textures. A smooth, flat surface like that of a polished marble or wood has low friction, where as something like sandpaper has high friction. In this case the cup rolls away quickly on the concrete because it is smoother than the carpet (less friction). The cup slows down once it hits the carpet because there is more resistance to its motion due to higher friction between two surfaces (the bottom of the cup ($c$) touching with top surface of carpet($s_1$)).\nSo answer will be "concrete floor".', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
