question: 38, answer 445 {'source': 'In this task, you are given two strings A, B. Find the longest common substring in the strings A and B.\n\nYGuQYlZN, JIQYluk', 'target': 'QYl', 'rationale': 'To find the longest common substring, you have to consider all substrings in each string. For example, let\'s take string A and B, YGuQYlZN and JIQYluk.\\n\\nString A:\\n1. "Y" : No match with string B -> Ignore this substring.\\n2. "G" : No match with string B -> Ignore this substring.\\n3."u": No match with string B -> Ignore this substring\\n4."Q" : Match with \'Q\' in stringB -> Max length of common substring is 1 (until now). We can\'t remove any character from either side of the matched characters because both strings ends after \'Q\'. Also there are no other matches from now on so we can stop processing further substrings for StringA and begin processing StringB\'s substrings if any (we will see that there isn\'t). Current max length is still 1 so move to next step without updating it yet (because we will see if there is a longer one later)\\n5."Y": Match with \'Y\' in StringB -> Max length of common substring is 2 since both strings contains "YY". Again since both strings end here we can stop processing further substrings for StringA and begin processing StringB\'s substrings if any (we will see that there isn\'t). Current max length is 2 so update it as new max value (\'YY\') \\nb)String B:\\no1: "JI": No match with \'JI\' in A->Ignore this Substring o2: Q: Matches at same index as Q in A->MaxLength=1(including current char) since only one character matches but since no more matching characters after this point stop here & update current max value(\'Q\') o3:"l":NoMatchwithstrinA->IgnorethisSubstring', 'task': 'synthetic', 'type': 'CoT'}
