question: 55, answer 99 {'source': 'Water, while a finite resource, is renewable because\n\nA -> water is good to drink\n\nB -> water is hard to dry up\n\nC -> water is quite cyclical\n\nD -> water is found in trees\n\nIs the right answer A, B, C or D ?', 'target': 'C', 'rationale': 'The water cycle describes the movement of water between land, oceans and sky. As a result, although there is only so much moisture on our planet at any one time (i.e., it\'s in finite supply), this "stock" can be replenished by evaporation: when evaporated ocean water condenses into clouds and falls as rain or snow onto the land. This process makes water renewable rather than nonrenewable; C is therefore correct!', 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
