question: 64, answer 135 {'source': 'The rate of growth for a species of grass was measured in a treeless yard and tree-shaded yard. The grass grew twice as fast in the treeless yard. Which factor most likely contributed to the difference in growth rate?\n\nOptions:\n- amount of animals\n- amount of light\n- amount of soil\n- amount of rain', 'target': 'amount of light', 'rationale': 'The rate of growth for a species of grass was measured in treeless yard and tree-shaded yard. The grass grew twice as fast in the treeless yard, so it is reasonable to assume that there has been more sunlight available in the former than latter since trees naturally shade their surrounding areas from direct sun rays. \nAmong the options provided, such as amount of animals; amount of soil; and amount of rain, none are likely factors affecting plant growth except light (sunlight). Therefore, "amount of light" should be selected as an answer because it most likely contributed to difference in growth rate between two yards which were observed by scientists or whoever made this question/problem.', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Challenge', 'type': 'CoT'}
