question: 54, answer 89 {'source': 'Pick the most correct option to answer the following question.\n\nEvaporation, condensation, and precipitation are all processes which occur in the\n\nOptions:\n\n- A: water cycle.\n\n- B: energy cycle.\n\n- C: carbon cycle.\n\n- D: nitrogen cycle.', 'target': 'A', 'rationale': 'The answer is A.\nThe processes of evaporation, condensation and precipitation are all part of the water cycle where liquid water evaporates from land or sea as a gas called water vapor, tiny droplets collect in clouds where they might become raindrops (precipitation) that fall back to earth, then it goes through an underground aquifer system before returning again to lakes, seas and oceans which will start the process over again.', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Easy', 'type': 'CoT'}
