question: 111, answer 168 {'source': "Yep . I burned myself with not only dry ice ... but dry ice and acetone ... That 's -270 degrees F. Yeah . It hurt . Fortunately , I think it will be okay .\nAccording to the above context, choose the best option to answer the following question.\nQuestion: What will the narrator do next after the mishap ?\nOptions:\nA. They will apply some aloe .\nB. They will apply a band aid .\nC. They will apply some dry ice .\nD. None of the above choices .", 'target': 'A', 'rationale': 'The narrator states that they burned themselves with dry ice and acetone. Based on the context, it can be inferred that a chemical compound was used by the speaker to cool something down (likely in reference to a science experiment). The speaker then says "Yeah... It hurt" implying their burns were painful. Dry ice is an extremely cold solid form of carbon dioxide (-109 degrees Fahrenheit), so burning oneself would likely cause severe pain or tissue damage similar to frostbite.\nDry ice should not be applied directly onto human skin as this will worsen any injury caused from exposure to dry ice or other extreme temperatures. Therefore, applying some aloe would help reduce pain and swelling if the person\'s skin had been affected by exposure to dry ice which makes A \nthe best answer choice for what the', 'task': 'cosmos_qa', 'type': 'CoT'}
