question: 166, answer 191 {'source': "In this task, you are given a short story consisting of exactly 5 sentences where the second sentence is missing. You are given two options and you need to select the one that best connects the first sentence with the rest of the story. Indicate your answer by 'Option 1' if the first option is correct, otherwise 'Option 2'. The incorrect option will change the subsequent storyline, so that at least one of the three subsequent sentences is no longer consistent with the story.\n\nSentence 1: Little Timmy wanted to grow up to be a race car driver. \n Sentence 3: On his seventh birthday his parents bought him a set of toy cars \n Sentence 4:  He loved them \n Sentence 5:  He still plays with them to this day \n Option 1: But he died before he was 7. \n Option 2: He always dreamed of joining F1 racing.", 'target': 'Option 2', 'rationale': 'In the first three sentences, it is explained that Timmy wanted to be a race car driver. He received toy cars as his birthday present and loved them. These sentences fit well together because they are explaining how much he liked cars. In the fourth sentence, it is mentioned that he still plays with them to this day. Since this sentence refers back to the third sentence (where he got toy race cars for his birthday), we can assume that Timmy is still playing with these toys at a later time (e.g., 10 years old). This creates a timeline for all of these events, in which case Option 1 does not make sense since it implies Timmy died on his 7th birthday before getting any toys from his parents. Thus, Option 2 would be correct since there was no mention of him dying in any part of the story and we know that he received some F1 car toys when he turned 7 years old (based on Sentence 3).', 'task': 'synthetic', 'type': 'CoT'}
