question: 56, answer 95 {'source': 'Answer the question based on the following text.\n\nQuestion:\n\n\nIf Mona is freezing a glass of water and the temperature of the water begins to decrease, what happens to the density of that water increases or decreases? \n\n\nText:\n\nLower temperature and higher salinity yield the densest water.', 'target': 'increases', 'rationale': 'Density is a measure of the amount of mass per unit volume. As water freezes, it expands in size (volume). However, since its temperature dropped as well, this expansion could not have caused its density to increase. Therefore, since for ice at 0°C and 1 atmosphere pressure has a density greater than that of liquid water at the same conditions; we can conclude that when freezing occurs, an object\'s overall density increases.\nSo answer is "increases"', 'task': 'quartz', 'type': 'CoT'}
