question: 52, answer 102 {'source': "Two meteorologists study Earth's climate. Jerry studies alpine climate, while James studies tropical climates. They both made great progress.\n\nGiven the paragraph above, please answer correctly the following question: \n\nWhich person learned less about the dry adiabatic lapse rate?", 'target': 'James', 'rationale': 'The dry adiabatic lapse rate is the change in air temperature with height when no water vapor or other substances are present. It occurs because as a parcel of air rises, it expands and cools at about 10°C for every 1000 meters (3281 ft) gained in elevation until the dew point is reached.\nThis phenomenon pertains to tropical climates more than alpine ones since there\'s generally less moisture available for condensation", so James learned less about this subject compared to Jerry.', 'task': 'ropes', 'type': 'CoT'}
