question: 82, answer 127 {'source': 'I gave my students this multiple choice question: Drew knows that Earth is tilted on its axis. He also knows this tilt is responsible for the season that a region on Earth will experience. When the South Pole is tilted toward the Sun, what season will it be in Florida?\n\nOnly one answer is correct among these 4 choices:\n- fall\n- spring\n- summer\n- winter\n\nCould you tell me which one is correct?', 'target': 'winter', 'rationale': 'The angle of the Earth\'s axis relative to its orbital plane is responsible for creating seasons on the planet. \nWhen a hemisphere tilts toward or away from the Sun, it experiences summer and winter, respectively. The tilt of Earth\'s rotation allows both hemispheres to experience spring and fall once in each orbit around the sun.\nBecause Drew knows that Earth is tilted on an axis, when South Pole is tilted toward he Sun (winter), Florida will be experiencing winter as well because they are in different hemispheres.\n\n\nTherefore, "Winter" would be correct answer choice among these 4 choices: Fall/Spring/Summer/Winter.', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Challenge', 'type': 'CoT'}
