question: 56, answer 157 {'source': 'Use information from the paragraph to answer the question.\n\nQuestion:\n\n\nAs we fill a balloon with air the number of reactions in the balloon increase or decrease? \n\n\nParagraph :\n\nAt higher concentrations, particles of reactants are crowded closer together, so they are more likely to collide and react.', 'target': 'increase', 'rationale': 'The paragraph explains that when the concentration of a substance increases, so does the number of collisions between reactant particles. As we fill a balloon with air and increase its volume, there is more space for molecules to occupy inside it. Therefore, at higher volumes the concentration (number per unit area) decreases. Since this results in fewer collisons between reactants, then their reaction rate also must decrease as well; hence option A cannot be correct:\nincrease --> incorrect \nIt follows that since decreasing concentrations will always result in less frequent collisions and therefore lower reaction rates, then if an opposite situation occurs where increasing concentrations lead to increased frequency of collisions and thus faster reactions are observed - then by default these two opposing situations mean than whenever concentrations increase -> reaction rates MUST DECREASE! So B', 'task': 'quartz', 'type': 'CoT'}
