question: 109, answer 161 {'source': 'Goal: Ride a bicycle.\n\nWhich is the correct ending?\n- Hold the bicycle upright between your legs with one foot on a pedal. Gently push off the ground with your other foot and place it on the other pedal, then apply pressure to the pedals with the feet to continue forward motion.\n- Hold the bicycle upright between your legs with both feet on a pedals. Gently push off the ground with your other foot and place it on the other pedal, then apply pressure to the pedals with the feet to continue forwards motion.\n\nAnswer:', 'target': 'Hold the bicycle upright between your legs with one foot on a pedal. Gently push off the ground with your other foot and place it on the other pedal, then apply pressure to the pedals with the feet to continue forward motion.', 'rationale': 'The correct answer is:\n\n  - Hold the bicycle upright between your legs with one foot on a pedal. Gently push off the ground with your other foot and place it on the other pedal, then apply pressure to the pedals with the feet to continue forward motion..\n  \nReasoning: In order to ride a bike, you need both hands free at some point in time so that you can steer (i.e., hold onto handlebars). Since there are only two feet but three necessary items (two handlebars and one seat), it would be impossible for someone who does not have prior experience riding a bike to get going if they had their first use of each item simultaneously (both feet on pedals). Furthermore, since placing both feet down again would require stopping completely before resuming', 'task': 'piqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
