question: 68, answer 307 {'source': 'In this task you will be given a string and you should find the longest substring that is a palindrome. A palindrome is a string that is the same backwards as it is forwards. If the shortest possible palindrome is length 1 you should return the first character.\n\nslssxsllsll', 'target': 'llsll', 'rationale': 'Given the string \'slssxsllsll\', let\'s look at each character.\\n1. \'s\' is not a palindrome.\\n2. \'l\' is not a palindrome.\\n3. \'s\' is not a palindrome either, but looking backwards we can see that it matches with the first \'s\'. This makes it possible to form the longest substring that is a palindrome: "slss". However, note that we should return the longest substring possible, so this isn\'t our answer yet!\\n4. The next character is an x, which doesn\'t make any difference in forming our palindromic substring so far ("slss"). Therefore, this character simply isn\'t used in creating our final result!\\n5 & 6 (the remaining characters). We have finally reached another sub-palindromic string: "ll". Now since there are no more characters left to check and since this string has the same length as "s", we know that we cannot find any longer strings than these two candidates (unless they happen to be one of these two exactly). Since both candidates are equally long and equally valid (both are single-character substrings), we will choose lexicographically higher of them ("ll" > "s"), which gives us our final answer: ll', 'task': 'synthetic', 'type': 'CoT'}
