question: 70, answer 213 {'source': 'The task is to generate text based off of an event. For the given event, there will be a person who does the action in the event (usually PersonX). Your task is to write that persons intent behind doing the event, i.e. why did the person do that action.\n\nPersonX makes a ___ upon PersonY', 'target': 'to show off', 'rationale': 'The event is PersonX making an impression upon PersonY. An impression can be seen as the effect that something has on a person, and they can be positive, negative, or neutral. It seems like it would not make sense for a person to make an impression on another person if they were trying to have no effect at all (a neutral impression), so we need to determine whether the intent of PersonX was positive or negative.\\nMaking an impression could mean that someone wants others to like them, which is typically seen as having a positive intent behind it. However in this case there are no other details about what sort of impression PersonX made on PersonY so it is hard to know whether their intent was actually positive or not. We can however assume that if the phrase "to show off" applies in this situation then PersonX\'s intention was most likely negative because showing off generally does not make others like you very much; rather it just makes people think you are arrogant and annoying (i.e., having a negative effect).', 'task': 'event2mind', 'type': 'CoT'}
