question: 99, answer 152 {'source': "I spent most of it with Clark . He wanted to go out so we decided we 'd go round town and then head off somewhere . We did a little shopping and I brought him this new jacket and belt ( because I ' m nice like that ) and he was being overly nice .\nWhat may Clark do in town ?\nA. He bought me a few things .\nB. None of the above choices .\nC. He went to a few stores .\nD. He stayed somewhere in town .", 'target': 'C', 'rationale': 'The context is a conversation between two friends, in which the speaker mentions that they went shopping with their friend Clark. The speaker then says that she bought Clark a new jacket and belt because "I’m nice like that". This suggests that although both of them did some shopping together there are no indications as to whether or not Clark purchased anything for her.\nBased on this, it can be inferred from the given information stated above (i.e., going round town) we can conclude that he might have gone to few stores but nowhere else since being overly nice does definitely rule out staying somewhere in town or buying things for her (see A & D). Hence C - “He went to few stores” is correct answer choice here!', 'task': 'cosmos_qa', 'type': 'CoT'}
