question: 94, answer 101 {'source': 'I gave my students this multiple choice question: Roger visited his grandfather who lives on a farm. While he was there, he helped his grandfather move hay out of the barn. As Roger worked in the barn he began sneezing. Which system of the body most likely caused Roger to sneeze?\n\nOnly one answer is correct among these 4 choices:\n- circulatory\n- excretory\n- digestive\n- immune\n\nCould you tell me which one is correct?', 'target': 'immune', 'rationale': 'The most likely reason for a person to sneeze is that they are being exposed to an irritant and the immune system responds by causing them to reflexively sneeze in order to clear their airway of dust, pollen or other particles. This means it\'s probably not because Roger was working with hay (his digestive system), washing farm equipment (excretory) or visiting his grandfather (circulatory).\nTherefore, the correct answer should be "immune".', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Easy', 'type': 'CoT'}
