question: 61, answer 156 {'source': 'Here\'s a short story: A plane stays much cooler taxing through a hanger than taxing over a runway. The plane will move a greater distance over (A) runway (B) hanger.\n\nWhat is the most sensical answer between "hanger" and  "runway"?', 'target': 'runway', 'rationale': 'The story is about an airplane taxing through a hanger and then over a runway. The rationale given to choose "runway" as the answer:\nA plane stays much cooler taxing through a hangar than taxing over a runway." Taxing means moving at low speed, so it\'s clear that we\'re talking about ground movement here (not flying). A hangar is indoors where there are walls around you for protection from heat/cold. So taking off or landing in such conditions will be less stressful on your body because of the temperature being controlled inside. But when you go out into open air with no barriers (like running), your body has to work harder to regulate its temperature by itself - therefore it would get hotter faster if exposed longer.', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
