question: 99, answer 111 {'source': 'Q: What is harmless water vapor, for a powerplant?\n\n\nRead this paragraph and choose the correct option from the provided answers:\n\nSteam rises from the cooling towers of this nuclear power plant. The steam is only harmless water vapor. Unlike a power plant that burns fossil fuel, a nuclear power plant doesn’t release pollution into the air. That’s because a nuclear power plant produces power by nuclear fission, a type of nuclear reaction.\n\n Choices:\n\n- wind\n\n- plasma\n\n- fog\n\n- steam\n\n\nA:', 'target': 'steam', 'rationale': 'Steam is water that has been heated to the point where it starts to turn into a gas. In this case, steam rises from cooling towers of nuclear power plants. The paragraph states that unlike other fossil fuel-burning power plants, nuclear power plants do not release pollution into the air because they use fission instead of burning fossil fuels. This means that any vapor released by them must be harmless as well; thus, in this context “steam” would be considered harmless and safe for humans to breathe if inhaled or ingested\nSo the answer is "steam".', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
