question: 54, answer 127 {'source': 'Here\'s a logic test: The empty cement truck weighed less than the full cement truck so it was _____ when it was accelerating (A) faster (B) slower\n\nChoose the answer between "Empty cement truck" and "Full cement truck".', 'target': 'Empty cement truck', 'rationale': 'The question mentions an empty cement truck and a full one. The first sentence says that the empty one weighs less than the full truck, which means it has less mass. Given this information, Newton’s second law of motion tells us that if all else is equal (net force), then acceleration will be inversely proportional to mass; bigger masses have smaller accelerations, while smaller ones have larger accelerations. This means that given constant net forces between two objects with different masses, the lighter object will accelerate faster than the heavier object—just as stated by option A: Empty cement truck\nSo answer is "Empty Cement Truck".', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
