question: 154, answer 325 {'source': "In this task, you are given an input list. A list contains several comma-separated items written within brackets. You need to return the count of all the numerical elements in the given list. Return 0 if no numerical element in the list.\n\n['8365', 'P', '4629', 's', '4185', '5619', 'W', '1987', '8075', 'S', 't', 'd', '6921', '6465', '4121', 'Q', 'n', '8047', 'A', 'l', 'W', '4943', '2855']", 'target': '12', 'rationale': "In the given list, all numerical elements are as followings.\\n1. 8365\\n2. 4629\\n3. 4185\\n4. 5619\\n5. 1987\\n6. 8075\\n7. 6921\\n8, 9, 10 and 11 are all letters or symbols so they will be converted into 0 during the final calculation process \\nd12 is 6921 which is a number, but it will be converted into 0 during the final calculation process because it's not in the range of 1 to 20 \\nd13 is 6465 which is a number, but it will be converted into 0 during the final calculation process because it's not in the range of 1 to 20 \\nd14 is 4121 which is a number, but it will be converted into 0 during the final calculation process because it's not in the range of 1 to 20 \\nd15 and 16 are Q and n respectively so they will both be converted into 0 during final calculation proceess (because only alphabetical characters with values between A-Z can convert numbers; any other characters such as Q or n cannot do this)\\nd17 = 8047 -> this one can convert back to 7126 based on our rules (an alternate way of doing this would have been applying our rule for E -> 5 first then applying our rule for S -> 6 second)\n\nThe total count after conversion would therefore become: 8365 + 4629 + 4185 + 5619 + 1987 + 8075 + 7126 = 38876", 'task': 'synthetic', 'type': 'CoT'}
