question: 111, answer 116 {'source': 'In this task, you will be shown a short story with a beginning, two potential middles, and an ending. Your job is to choose the middle statement that makes the story coherent / plausible by writing "1" or "2" in the output. If both sentences are plausible, pick the one that makes most sense.\n\nBeginning: Chuck was startled when he felt his stomach rumble. Middle 1: Chuck realized that it was very early. Middle 2: Chuck realized that it was very late. Ending: He had just worked past dinner as well.', 'target': '2', 'rationale': "In the beginning of the story, Chuck is startled by a rumble in his stomach. It is thus most plausible that he realizes that it is very late, because this indicates why his stomach rumbled. If he realized it was very early (Middle 1), then there would be no reason to explain why his stomach rumbled unless Chuck woke up late and therefore had not eaten breakfast yet. Middle 2 provides a more reasonable explanation for why Chuck's stomach rumbled than Middle 1, so we choose Middle 2 as the middle sentence that makes most sense in light of the beginning and ending sentences.", 'task': 'abductive_nli', 'type': 'CoT'}
