question: 85, answer 118 {'source': 'Here\'s a short story: Terry was playing with a bag of marbles. He put a marble on a wooden table and flicked it off. Then he put the marble on the rougher carpet and flicked it again. The marble on the _____ moved faster. (A) wooden table (B) carpet.\n\nWhat is the most sensical answer between "carpet" and  "wooden table"?', 'target': 'carpet', 'rationale': 'When Terry flicked the marble on a wooden table, it moved slowly. The reason for this is that wood has high friction and so does not allow an object to move easily along its surface. When Terry then placed the marble on carpet, he found that when he flicked it again, the same type of motion took place but at a faster speed than before. This shows us that marbles will travel much more quickly over carpets because there is less frictional force opposing their movement compared with moving them across surfaces such as tables (which are smoother).\nSo we choose "carpet" here.', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
