question: 21, answer 157 {'source': 'Answer the question...which city was known as porkopolis after its slaughterhouse district??', 'target': 'Cincinnati, Ohio', 'rationale': 'THe first city to establish a meat packing district was Cincinnati, Ohio. The districts were located near the banks of rivers so that animals could be transported easily from rural areas. \nThe main reason for this is because pork and beef are perishable items that can only last so long before spoiling without refrigeration technologies. It would have been very difficult for cities to import meat products in an age where shipping technology did not exist yet. In addition, meat processing required large amounts of water which also necessitated locating these facilities on riverbanks with access to clean drinking water.\nCincinnati became known as Porkopolis due its location along the Miami-Erie Canal providing easy transport routes between farms and slaughterhouses in southwestern Ohio and other major markets like Chicago or New York City via Lake Michigan and', 'task': 'natural_questions', 'type': 'CoT'}
