question: 63, answer 124 {'source': 'Choose between "clogged toilet" and  "clean toilet".\nQuestion: A plunger gets a lot hotter plunging through a clogged toilet then plunging through a clean toilet. Which surface will let the plunger go a greater distance per push? (A) clogged toilet (B) clean toilet', 'target': 'clean toilet', 'rationale': 'The plunger gets a lot hotter plunging through a clogged toilet then plunging through a clean toilet, which means the surface of the clean toilet transfers heat more efficiently. This implies that it has lower thermal resistance than that of the clogged one. Hence, its temperature will be higher at any given instant for an equal push on both toilets. Since power = force x velocity and since all other forces are equal, greater speed is needed to generate same amount of energy from the cleaner plunger hence making it travel further in comparison with less distance covered by dirty/clogged one per unit time or per push.', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
