question: 71, answer 144 {'source': 'I gave my students this multiple choice question: Which of these processes can cause layers of rock to be arranged so that the youngest layers are found below older layers?\n\nOnly one answer is correct among these 4 choices:\n- melting and hardening\n- cooling and heating\n- deposition and cementing\n- uplifting and faulting\n\nCould you tell me which one is correct?', 'target': 'uplifting and faulting', 'rationale': 'The process of uplifting and faulting can cause layers of rock to be arranged so that the youngest layers are found below older layers.\nUplifting refers to a geologic action in which blocks or sections of Earth\'s crust rise vertically by forces within the planet, resulting in new land surfaces above sea level. Uplifted areas may be eroded over time because they are higher than surrounding regions and this erosion deposits sediment onto buried rocks along faults (a break or fracture between two tectonic plates). \nWhen combined with faulting, these processes result in an arrangement where younger sediments lie on top of older ones.\n\n\nTherefore, from among all answer choices "uplifting and faulting" is correct one for the question asked.', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Challenge', 'type': 'CoT'}
