question: 28, answer 138 {'source': 'Which would likely live under a rock?\n\nChoose an answer from this list:\n- an eagle\n- a cat\n- a vole\n- a dog', 'target': 'a vole', 'rationale': 'The vole is a small rodent adapted to living in underground burrows or under rocks. Voles are active all year round, even during cold weather and heavy snowfall. They live for two years on average, but some survive up to four years in the wild. A rock provides protection from predators such as eagles and cats; it also offers shelter from bad weather conditions like rain and wind that might otherwise damage their nests. In addition to this, voles can find food sources near rocks because they eat seeds found beneath them - something which would not be possible if there were no stones around at all!\nSo based on these facts we know that "a vole" lives under a rock.', 'task': 'openbookqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
