question: 49, answer 93 {'source': 'Q: Sickle-cell disease significantly impairs the function of what?\n\n\nRead this paragraph and choose the correct option from the provided answers:\n\n\n\n Choices:\n\n- limbic system\n\n- nervous system\n\n- metabolism system\n\n- circulatory system\n\n\nA:', 'target': 'circulatory system', 'rationale': 'Sickle-cell disease is a blood disorder caused by abnormal hemoglobin, which can lead to sickle-shaped red blood cells. These deformed cells are not able to effectively carry oxygen throughout the body and become stuck in small blood vessels. This obstructs circulation and limits the amount of oxygen available for cellular respiration, leading to tissue damage. Sickle-cell disease significantly impairs the function of the circulatory system', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
