question: 45, answer 92 {'source': 'Q: What the name of the disease where some of the alveoli of the lungs fill with fluid so they can no longer exchange gas?\n\n\n Choices:\n\n- leukemia\n\n- lung cancer\n\n- emphysema\n\n- pneumonia\n\nA:', 'target': 'pneumonia', 'rationale': 'The alveoli are the tiny pockets in your lungs where oxygen is exchanged for carbon dioxide. This exchange of gases happens when you breathe in and out, so it’s important that they stay healthy! In pneumonia, some of these small sacs fill with fluid instead of air. As a result, less gas can be transferred between the blood and breath. Pneumonia is therefore caused by an inability to transfer gas through the alveoli; The answer: pneumonia', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
