question: 86, answer 121 {'source': 'Use information from the paragraph to answer the question.\n\nParagraph :\n\nThe closer to the surface an aquifer is, the easier it is to get the water.\n\nQuestion:\n\n\nA group of settlers decided to live close to one aquifer instead of another aquifer because the aquifer they chose was much farther from the surface. Getting water from the aquifer farther from the surface will be easier or more difficult.?', 'target': 'more difficult.', 'rationale': 'The paragraph states that the closer to the surface an aquifer is, the easier it is to get water from it. The question mentions two aquifers and asks which one will be easier or more difficult to get water from. It also says that settlers chose live close to one of them instead of another because they wanted a location farther away from the surface. This means that chosen aquifer was further down in relation to its surroundings than another one, making it more difficult for people living nearby to access their water sources. So we can say with certainty "more difficult." is correct answer here', 'task': 'quartz', 'type': 'CoT'}
