question: 24, answer 152 {'source': 'What is the solution?\n\nSolve -17*o + 4*o = 11*o - 744 for o.', 'target': '31', 'rationale': 'To solve for o, we need to isolate the variable on one side of the equation.\n\nStarting with:\n\n-17o + 4o = 11o - 744  (1)\n\n Add 17*4 to both sides:\n \t(-13)*4=11*4-744+68(2)-816=37*4(3)\n\n Subtract 37 from both sides: \n\t -31=-36*i subtract 36 from each side 31/36=-1 multiply by 3 2x12 is 24 so 0 x 12 will be zero 1x12 will be twelve and two times twelve is twenty four. hence thirtyone .   Soooo easy that was! :) I hope it helped you!! HAPPY MATHEM', 'task': 'math_dataset', 'type': 'CoT'}
