question: 125, answer 166 {'source': "In this task, you're given the middle and ending of a three-part story. Your job is to complete the short story by writing a probable beginning of the story. Generated sentences must be short, have fewer than 10 words, and be simple as if narrating to a child. Avoid using any irrelevant extra information when creating the beginning, and use names (e.g. Jack, Barbara,...) instead of pronouns (e.g. he / she) wherever possible.\n\nMiddle: Dinner tasted very bad. Ending: Needless to say, I won't use that recipe again.", 'target': 'I made meatloaf and homemade macaroni and cheese for supper', 'rationale': 'The middle of the story states that dinner tasted bad, so we can infer that the protagonist cooked dinner for themselves. The ending implies that this was an intentional act; it is unlikely that the protagonist is a victim of poisoning, and if they were, it wouldn\'t be relevant to their decision not to use the recipe again. Therefore, we can conclude that the protagonist cooked dinner for themselves and did not like how it turned out. A probable beginning would be \\"I made meatloaf and homemade macaroni and cheese for supper\\" because this provides more information about what happened during dinner time in a simple way without including irrelevant extra information like \\"I got home from work at 6pm\\" or \\"The food didn\'t taste bad at first but after two hours I felt sick\\".', 'task': 'abductive_nli', 'type': 'CoT'}
