question: 57, answer 115 {'source': 'I gave my students this multiple choice question: Which land form results when carbonic acid in groundwater seeps through rock and dissolves limestone?\n\nOnly one answer is correct among these 4 choices:\n- valleys\n- ravines\n- caverns\n- mountains\n\nCould you tell me which one is correct?', 'target': 'caverns', 'rationale': 'A land form that results when carbonic acid in groundwater seeps through rock and dissolves limestone is a cavern. A ravine could also result from water erosion of the earth, but it would not be formed as a direct consequence of the dissolution of limestone by acidic groundwater.\nValley refers to lowland between mountains or hills often with a river running through it; Caverns are natural underground spaces large enough for humans to enter. \n\n\nTherefore, "cavern" is correct answer among these choices: valleys, ravines, caverns and mountains.", so we should choose "Cavern".', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Easy', 'type': 'CoT'}
