question: 103, answer 221 {'source': "In this task, you need to answer the given multiple-choice question on the physics. Classify your answers into 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd', and 'e'.\n\nProblem: a and b together can do a work in 4 days . a alone can do it in 12 days . what time b will take to do the work alone ? \nOptions: a ) 6 days , b ) 8 days , c ) 12 days , d ) 10 days , e ) 5 days", 'target': 'a', 'rationale': 'Let a and b together can do (1/x) work in 1 day. So, a and b together can do 1/4 work in 4 days. Then, (a+b) x 4 = 1; therefore, x = 1/4.\\nSo, a and b together can do (1/4) work in one day. Hence, the speed of both of them is 4 units per day each.\\nSimilarly from the fact that \\"a alone can do it in 12 days\\", it follows that the speed of \\"a\\" is 3 units per day. \\nAlso from the fact that \\"speed of (a+b) is equal to sum of speeds of a and b\\", we get 3 + x = 4; hence, x = 1 unit per day ==> speed of \\"b\\" is also one unit per day. \\nTherefore time taken by \\"b\\" to complete the whole job alone will be 24 days i.e option A is correct answer', 'task': 'mathqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
