question: 82, answer 126 {'source': 'The exercise is to decide whether the question accepts the proposed suggestion as a correct answer. If yes, write "True", otherwise write "False".\nQuestion: when did thomson make the plum-pudding model\nSuggestion: In Thomson\'s model, electrons were free to rotate in rings which were further stabilized by interactions between the electrons, and spectra were to be accounted for by energy differences of different ring orbits.', 'target': 'False', 'rationale': 'The Plum-Pudding model is an alternative to the Rutherford atomic model that was proposed by J.J Thompson and later modified by Ernest Rutherford in 1911. According to this theory, electrons were present throughout a positively charged sphere called "Plum Pudding". \nThis suggestion describes Thomson\'s original plum pudding model (the one before being modified) but does not mention when he made it. So, while it mentions his version of the plum pudding model, since there\'s no information about when he came up with this idea specifically I would have to answer False because we\'re looking for something more specific than just any reference to his theory.', 'task': 'wiki_qa', 'type': 'CoT'}
