question: 53, answer 117 {'source': 'Choose between "clay court" and  "grass court".\nQuestion: Terri noticed that when serving the tennis ball it moved faster on the clay court than the grass court. This was because the grass court has (A) more resistance or (B) less resistance.', 'target': 'clay court', 'rationale': 'The tennis ball moves faster on the clay court than grass because of friction. When a moving object rubs against another surface there is resistance which causes heat and slows down that movement. Grass has little or no friction, so less resistance for the tennis ball to move fast on it. On the other hand, Clay Court being porous creates more friction with the Tennis Ball\'s rough outer skin causing more resistance in its movement resulting in slowing it down as compared to when playing on grass court.\nSince A - "more" corresponds to Clay Court; therefore, answer should be: clay court', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
