question: 28, answer 133 {'source': 'Does this phrase make sense?\nTo prevent dough from sticking to your hands, you can apply lemon juice to your hands\nAnswer with Yes or No', 'target': 'No', 'rationale': 'The phrase “To prevent dough from sticking to your hands, you can apply lemon juice to your hands” does not make sense. The answer is No. Dough contains baking powder and the function of baking powder is that it causes air bubbles in the dough so when heat comes into contact with these air bubbles it expands causing an increase in volume. So if we want our bread to rise then this process generally works well but when we are kneading our dough, applying any sort of acidic liquid such as vinegar or citrus will react violently and destroy all those precious little gas pockets which provide us good texture in our baked goods resulting a flatbread instead of a fluffy one.', 'task': 'piqa', 'type': 'CoT'}
