question: 98, answer 101 {'source': 'Question: I bought some smooth plastic furniture movers which let me push heavy furniture across my carpet on my own. I got tired of asking for help to rearrange the furniture, as before I bought these I couldn\'t do it alone. This was because the furniture movers (A) increased friction or (B) decreased friction?\n\nDo not use A and B to answer the question but instead, choose between "furniture movers on carpet" and  "furniture on carpet".', 'target': 'furniture on carpet', 'rationale': 'Friction is the force that resists motion when two objects are in contact. Here, friction between the furniture and carpet was making it difficult to move heavy pieces of furniture around on my own. To reduce this resistance, I bought plastic movers which have a lower coefficient of friction than wood or metal furniture legs would have on a carpeted floor (furniture on carpet). By reducing friction with these smooth plastic pads, I could now move large items without getting help from others (furniture movers on carpet)', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
