question: 80, answer 114 {'source': 'Here\'s a short story: Peter is playing with his ball inside the house. As he kicks the ball, the ball goes flying across the room and hits two bottles that are sitting on top of the table. Which bottle is more likely to break (A) plastic bottle (B) glass bottle.\n\nWhat is the most sensical answer between "glass bottle" and  "plastic bottle"?', 'target': 'plastic bottle', 'rationale': 'The answer is plastic bottle because glass bottles are made of a transparent material and the most commonly used for beverage containers. Since it has high transparency, glass can be recycled with relative ease compared to materials such as plastics which do not melt during the recycling process due to their molecular structure. Therefore, since plastic will eventually break down when exposed too much heat or pressure that comes from being inside an oven whereas glass won\'t crack so easily unless there\'s extreme force applied on them then this would make more sense in terms of logic behind why people choose one over another."', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
