question: 55, answer 110 {'source': 'Use information from the paragraph to answer the question.\n\nQuestion:\n\n\nIn tornadoes the less differences in air pressure cause lesser or stronger winds? \n\n\nParagraph :\n\nDifferences in air pressure over the surface of the Earth result in wind. The greater the differences in air pressures, the stronger the wind.', 'target': 'lesser', 'rationale': 'The paragraph states that differences in air pressure cause wind, and the greater these differences are, the stronger the corresponding winds will be. The question asks about tornadoes; during a tornado, there is an area of low pressure at its center called a mesocyclone. This means that if two locations have different pressures when compared to this relatively lower central region (as would typically be the case), then their difference in pressure must therefore be less than it otherwise would be.\nTherefore, the answer is “lesser” as opposed to "stronger".', 'task': 'quartz', 'type': 'CoT'}
