question: 67, answer 146 {'source': 'Pick the most correct option to answer the following question.\n\nWhich statement best identifies a living thing that depends on another living thing to survive?\n\nOptions:\n\n- A: A wolf drinks water.\n\n- B: A moose eats a plant.\n\n- C: A spruce tree grows in soil.\n\n- D: A salmonberry plant absorbs sunlight.', 'target': 'B', 'rationale': 'The moose eats a plant, and the salmonberry plant is eaten by animals.\nTherefore, an option “A” does not match with the question as it describes wolf drinking water rather than depending on other living thing to survive \n\n\nOption B: A moose eat plants. The statement best identifies that mooses are dependent upon plants for their food source; therefore they depend on another living things in order to continue surviving. Thus, the correct answer would be Option B: "A Moose Eats Plants".\n\n\nOptions C & D do not have any evidence of them being dependent upon anything else but themselves (examples include sunlight or soil). Therefore these options cannot be considered as correct answers as there is no proof stated within either option text suggesting otherwise.', 'task': 'ai2_arc@ARC-Easy', 'type': 'CoT'}
