question: 37, answer 62 {'source': 'Q: What causes natural ripening in fruit?\n\n\nRead this paragraph and choose the correct option from the provided answers:\n\n\n\n Choices:\n\n- sulfur\n\n- chloride\n\n- acid\n\n- ethylene\n\n\nA:', 'target': 'ethylene', 'rationale': 'Fruit ripening is the process in which fruit becomes sweeter, softer and develops its characteristic aroma. During this period of development, plants produce a hormone called ethylene that softens cell walls and increases sugar production. This causes fruits to soften and become ripe. The answer is therefore ethylene.', 'task': 'sciq', 'type': 'CoT'}
