question: 95, answer 148 {'source': 'Here\'s a logic test: Kaitlyn had a roll of tape and pushed it across the top of her metal freezer, then she pushed it across a floor mat. The roll of tape kept moving for a longer period of time on the metal freezer than it did on the floor mat. This is because there was more friction on the (A) metal freezer (B) floor mat.\n\nChoose the answer between "metal freezer" and "floor mat".', 'target': 'floor mat', 'rationale': 'Friction is the force that acts in a direction opposite to an object’s motion. In general, greater friction will reduce velocity (how fast something moves), and less friction will increase velocity. If there was more friction on the metal freezer than on the floor mat, then it would move slower across the top of the metal freezer than it did across the floor mat. Thus "floor mat" must be chosen as answer because Kaitlyn\'s roll of tape moved faster for longer period of time when she pushed it over this surface area compared to pushing it over another one; therefore, there had been less resistance from trying to push her roll of tape along this surface area compared with trying to push her roll of tape along another type .', 'task': 'quarel', 'type': 'CoT'}
