question: 39, answer 155 {'source': "where do you use a tourniquet temporarily?\nChoose the most suitable option to answer the above question.\nOptions:\n- doctor's office\n- ambulance\n- applying even pressure\n- hospital\n- emergency kit", 'target': 'ambulance', 'rationale': 'A tourniquet is used to control the blood flow in a limb such as an arm or leg. In emergency situations, it can be placed on someone who has suffered from severe bleeding in order to stop the bleeding and prevent them from losing too much blood. A tourniquet should only remain for about two hours before being removed because of the risk that nerve damage might occur if left on longer than this time period. This means that if you receive medical attention within two hours of using a tourniquet, your doctor will likely remove it right away once you arrive at their office or hospital care facility since they do not want any additional complications arising due to poor circulation of oxygenated blood while treating your injury.\nAn ambulance would often be where one ends up with a serious injury', 'task': 'cos_e', 'type': 'CoT'}
